    <br/>

    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#bbbbbb" width="1%" nowrap align="center">
            &nbsp;<font color="#ffffff"><b>Description</b></font>&nbsp;
        </td>
        <td>&nbsp;</td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p>As a platform administrator (RW-PLATADM), I want a feature flag service with each flag held as data (key, owner, value per environment, removal date) and read by the service and the front end at run time, so that a feature can be released switched off and switched on without a deployment, and no flag stays after its removal date without its owner being told.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <br/>

    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#bbbbbb" width="1%" nowrap align="center">
            &nbsp;<font color="#ffffff"><b>Comments</b></font>&nbsp;
        </td>
        <td>&nbsp;</td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="grid" style="margin: 0;">
                <tr id="comment-header-1793575"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="6125ab424f292300693a94df"
                id="word_commented_6125ab424f292300693a94df"
                href="https://scbjira.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=6125ab424f292300693a94df">
                    Ratchadaphorn Kasemphin
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">16/Nov/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-1793575"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://scbjira.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3Afef6ca03-d375-4fe4-83c9-f42b79051549" class="user-hover" rel="712020:fef6ca03-d375-4fe4-83c9-f42b79051549" data-account-id="712020:fef6ca03-d375-4fe4-83c9-f42b79051549" accountid="712020:fef6ca03-d375-4fe4-83c9-f42b79051549" rel="noreferrer">CHANISSARA MAHAKITTIKUN</a>  <br/>
cc. <a href="https://scbjira.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=634e23a1a04e906250c53a5f" class="user-hover" rel="634e23a1a04e906250c53a5f" data-account-id="634e23a1a04e906250c53a5f" accountid="634e23a1a04e906250c53a5f" rel="noreferrer">Chitchaya Muanchonchana</a> </p>

<p>After reviewing the card, I have the following concerns and questions that need clarification:</p>

<p><b>Concerns (Dependencies):</b> The card lists only RWB-E1-001 as a dependency. Several of its ACs and test cases also need the cards below to be completed first. All of them come later in the build sequence (this card is #16).</p>

<ul>
	<li><b>RWB-TE-007 (Scheduled jobs on Quartz, #21)</b> — provides the Quartz scheduler that runs the weekly flag report job (<tt>FlagRemovalReportJob</tt>, Monday 08:00 Asia/Bangkok). Without it, AC3 (Flag expiry) can only be tested by calling the job by hand, not as a scheduled run.</li>
	<li><b>RWB-E1-022 (Sign-on with SSO, MFA and the first roles, #26)</b> — provides sign-on and the Entra ID group to role mapping, for example RWB-UAT-RW-PLATADM to RW-PLATADM. Without it, there is no signed-in RW-PLATADM user to create or change flags, and GET /feature-flags cannot do its session check (401 / MSG-P4-001).</li>
	<li><b>RWB-E1-037 (Role to permission matrix and PDPA masking, #27)</b> — provides the "Platform administration" capability with C/R/U rights for each role. Without it, the endpoints cannot enforce access, so TC-E1-047-10 (RW-CASEOWN refused with 403 / MSG-P4-002) cannot be tested.</li>
	<li><b>RWB-E1-002 (#45) and RWB-E1-031 (#48)</b> — build SCR-02 Case list and its queue column. The reference flag <tt>rwb.casewf.case-list-queue-column</tt> hides and shows that column, so AC1, AC2 and the "Done when" condition (column hidden and shown in UAT without a deployment) cannot be tested end to end until these cards are done.</li>
	<li><b>ACE common module (external)</b> — AC2 needs the ACE audit log service, and the weekly report emails owners and the RW-PLATADM group through the ACE notification path for staff. We need confirmation that both are available in SIT and UAT, plus their API contracts.</li>
</ul>


<hr />

<p><b>Clarification needed:</b></p>

<p><b>1.Response shape of GET /feature-flags</b></p>

<p>The story's contract (section 12) says the response is a "Map of flag key to boolean for the caller's environment." API Specification v4 and TSD P2 (API-P2-005) define it as an array of <tt>FeatureFlagValue</tt>.</p>

<p><font color="#ff5630"><b>Question:</b></font> Which shape is correct? The <tt>useFeatureFlag</tt> hook and the contract tests depend on the answer.</p>

<p><b>2."Flag has no value set for UAT" (AC1)</b></p>

<p><b>AC1</b> starts with "the flag has no value set for UAT". The physical schema v6 defines <tt>uat_on boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT false</tt>, and Flow step 2 sets every environment to the default when the flag is created. So a "no value" state cannot exist in the data.</p>

<p><font color="#ff5630"><b>Question:</b> </font>Does AC1 mean "UAT still holds the default value <img class="emoticon" src="/images/icons/emoticons/lightbulb.png" height="16" width="16" align="absmiddle" alt="" border="0"/>"? If so, what is <tt>default_on</tt> used for after creation? Is it only the starting value, or does <tt>isOn()</tt> fall back to it in some cases?</p>

<p><b>3.Flag store unavailable after a restart (AC7, BR5)</b></p>

<p><b>AC7</b> and BR5 say that if the flag table cannot be read and there is no cached value (for example, after a restart), every flag returns off. In PROD, this means features that are already switched on would be switched off for users while the database is down.</p>

<p><font color="#ff5630"><b>Question:</b></font> Can we confirm that Business and Operational Risk accept this behaviour in PROD? If not, is a fallback in scope, such as the last known snapshot or a config file?</p>

<p><b>4.Flag key format validation</b></p>

<p>Flow step 2 checks the key pattern <tt>rwb.&lt;module&gt;.&lt;short-name&gt;</tt>, and the solution plan adds a check constraint <tt>^rwb\.<span class="error">&#91;a-z0-9&#93;</span><ins>\.<span class="error">&#91;a-z0-9-&#93;</span></ins>$</tt>. However:</p>

<ul>
	<li>No AC, exception path or test case covers an invalid key, for example <tt>RWB.P3.Test</tt> or <tt>rwb.p3</tt>.</li>
	<li>No AC or test case covers creating a flag whose key already exists. The contract lists 409 / MSG-GEN-004 for this.</li>
	<li>The examples mix naming styles: <tt>rwb.casewf.<b></tt>, <tt>rwb.p5.</b></tt>, <tt>rwb.p3.temporal</tt>.</li>
</ul>


<p><font color="#ff5630"><b>Questions:</b></font></p>

<ol>
	<li>What should the response be for an invalid key? 422 with which message ID?</li>
	<li>Should the <tt>&lt;module&gt;</tt> part be the module code (<tt>p3</tt>) or a short name (<tt>casewf</tt>)?</li>
</ol>




<p><b>5.Removal date boundaries</b></p>

<p>Exception X2 refuses a removal date "before today", and the weekly report lists flags with <tt>removal_date</tt> "before today."</p>

<p><font color="#ff5630"><b>Questions:</b> </font>Please confirm these two cases:</p>

<ol>
	<li>A flag created with removal date = today is accepted.</li>
	<li>A flag whose removal date = today (for example, a Monday report on the removal date itself) is <b>not</b> listed until the following Monday.</li>
</ol>


<p>Is there also a maximum allowed removal date, for example no more than 6 months ahead?</p>

<p><b>6.Retiring a flag and changing flag details</b></p>

<p>Section 10 says RW-PLATADM can retire flags, and the table has an <tt>is_active</tt> column. However, the contract has no endpoint for retiring a flag, and none for changing removal_date, owner or description after creation.</p>

<p><font color="#ff5630"><b>Questions:</b></font></p>

<ol>
	<li>Are retire and edit in scope for this story, or deferred to SCR-44 (Epic 8)?</li>
	<li>After a flag is retired, what does <tt>FeatureFlags.isOn()</tt> return: off, or the last value?</li>
	<li>Is a retired flag still allowed to stay in code without a warning?</li>
</ol>


<p><b>7.Changing a flag to the value it already has</b></p>

<p>The contract says "Setting the value it already has writes no change row," but no AC or test case covers this.</p>

<p><font color="#ff5630"><b>Questions:</b></font> Can we confirm the expected result when a flag is already on in UAT and the admin sends PATCH value=on again?</p>

<ul>
	<li>Is the response 200 with the unchanged flag?</li>
	<li>Does <tt>version</tt> stay the same?</li>
	<li>Is an ACE audit entry written?</li>
	<li>Is a reason still required?</li>
</ul>


<p><b>8.Weekly report rerun (idempotency)</b></p>

<p>The job contract says "Idempotency key: report date; a rerun on the same date sends nothing new." No table or column stores the report date, and the schema has no job-run table for this job.</p>

<p><font color="#ff5630"><b>Questions:</b></font></p>

<ol>
	<li>Where is the sent status stored for each report date?</li>
	<li>Can we confirm the expected result when the job is run again manually on the same Monday, both when the first run fully succeeded and when it partly failed (for example, one owner's email failed)?</li>
</ol>


<p><b>9.Change control for PROD</b></p>

<p>Section 10 gives RW-SECADM CRUDA rights on flags, which includes "A" (Approve). However, the flow has no approval step: any RW-PLATADM can switch a flag in PROD with only a reason.</p>

<p><font color="#ff5630"><b>Questions:</b></font></p>

<ol>
	<li>Do PROD flag changes need maker-checker approval, a change ticket reference, or a change window?</li>
	<li>If not, what is the "A" right of RW-SECADM used for in this story?</li>
</ol>

        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-1794302"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="712020:6b7673e3-795d-44f3-a9a5-f2348dbe7c53"
                id="word_commented_712020:6b7673e3-795d-44f3-a9a5-f2348dbe7c53"
                href="https://scbjira.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A6b7673e3-795d-44f3-a9a5-f2348dbe7c53">
                    Chanapai Gingpuwaluck
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">17/Nov/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-1794302"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>These points add to the questions already on this card.</p>

<ol>
	<li><b>The weekly flag report has no run book.</b> FlagRemovalReportJob is a new Quartz job, but it is not among the 16 <tt>job_catalog</tt> rows in RWB-E1-056. RunbookCompletenessTest ("every Quartz job has a run book") will fail unless the job is added.</li>
	<li><b>Front-end behaviour when the flag store is down.</b> The front end reads <tt>GET /feature-flags</tt> on page load, but the story does not say what it shows if the store is down. The 30-second cache is still an assumption under DL11, which is past due.</li>
	<li><b>Allowed module names.</b> Please list the allowed <tt>&lt;module&gt;</tt> values (module code such as <tt>p3</tt>, or short name such as <tt>casewf</tt>), so that the key check has a fixed list.</li>
	<li><b>Typo.</b> AC4 has a typo: "does not creat".</li>
</ol>


<p>Who answers: Tech lead, Henka (BA).</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-1794418"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="712020:e1a21d87-932c-4c28-81e8-8569a0d090a1"
                id="word_commented_712020:e1a21d87-932c-4c28-81e8-8569a0d090a1"
                href="https://scbjira.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3Ae1a21d87-932c-4c28-81e8-8569a0d090a1">
                    Nuttapon Jittachotisak
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">17/Nov/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
